WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:03.549
Roll up, roll up, come one and all!

00:00:03.549 --> 00:00:05.770
The circus is in town!

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:11.709
And not just any circus: the greatest show
in all the multiverse!

00:00:11.709 --> 00:00:15.780
Don't pay attention to the fact that the tents
weren't here yesterday, or that you don't

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:18.820
remember hearing anything about it before
now.

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:25.230
That's just the circus magic at work, and
there's no circus more magical or more mysterious

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:27.910
than Herman Fuller's Circus of the Disquieting!

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:35.320
It’s a show so marvelous that even the SCP
Foundation wants to get in on the act!

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:38.570
So come watch the show, come feel the magic!

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:42.320
After all… what do you have to lose?

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:48.760
The story of this humble traveling show begins
in 1893, with the founder, Herman S. Fuller.

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:54.470
He was born into a wealthy family, and at
the age of 21, he was invited by his uncle

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:59.080
to Chicago to see the buildings his company
had constructed for the world's fair.

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:04.000
He was dazzled by the sights he saw in the
windy city, and from then on he dedicated

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:10.680
his life to finding a way to bring that same
awe to people across America, and eventually,

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:12.050
the world.

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:16.390
After receiving a small loan from his uncle,
Herman Fuller set about building the miraculous

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:19.090
circus you see before you today!

00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:24.229
He knew he had to get a leg up over his competitors
- after all, the 1890's were a golden age

00:01:24.229 --> 00:01:26.200
for traveling shows in America.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:31.770
So, Herman devoted his time to research, trying
to find acts and oddities that were truly

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:33.240
out of this world.

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:38.190
He learned the way between worlds, stole books
from the Wanderer's Library, and with them

00:01:38.190 --> 00:01:44.350
studied alchemy, transmutation, sarkism, and
other supernatural disciplines.

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:48.610
That real magic and touch of the macabre would
be what made Herman Fuller's Circus of the

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:53.799
Disquieting so special, and would ultimately
give it its longevity.

00:01:53.799 --> 00:01:59.299
Herman Fuller's first anomalous acquisition
was a genuine Fiji Mermaid, like the one that

00:01:59.299 --> 00:02:00.560
famed showman P.T.

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:04.119
Barnum kept on display around the same time
period.

00:02:04.119 --> 00:02:08.410
Unlike Barnum's, however, Fuller's mermaid
had been brought to life.

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:13.630
The crowds loved it, but like all attractions,
pretty soon crowds grew bored of it and hungered

00:02:13.630 --> 00:02:19.540
for the next strange sight, so Fuller went
about acquiring more curiosities.

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:24.950
His next important acquisition was the man
with the upside-down face, or 'Manny' for

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:25.950
short.

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:31.440
He serves as second-in-command to the ringmaster,
and manages things behind the scenes, including

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:34.450
the acquisition of new talent.

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:38.050
Many other anomalous beings and items were
purchased for the circus by Fuller through

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:43.531
the auction company known as Marshall, Carter
and Dark - another group that the SCP Foundation

00:02:43.531 --> 00:02:46.290
makes a habit of keeping tabs on.

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:51.290
Another thing that sets this circus apart
from any other is the clowns, because they

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:54.100
aren’t like any you’ve ever seen before!

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:59.020
Though Herman Fuller's Circus of the Disquieting
employs professional clowns, the vast majority

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:05.870
of the Clown troupe are non-human, descendants
of an extradimensional race of magical shapeshifters.

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:10.090
Nobody really knows why they decided to come
to our reality and help Herman Fuller set

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:15.120
up his circus, but the leading theory is simply
that they were bored.

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:19.319
These original Clowns are the progenitors
of the “turned Clowns” and the “bred

00:03:19.319 --> 00:03:24.450
Clowns” - turned Clowns being humans who
underwent a Clown transformation procedure,

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:30.050
and the bred Clowns being artificially-grown
children produced by the other two types.

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:34.590
Earlier in the circus' history, before we
knew what we know today about genetics, much

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:40.590
more barbaric methods were used to create
new clowns - young human subjects would be

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:47.879
subjected to beatings and painful transfigurations
at the hands of the circus' Child-Breaker.

00:03:47.879 --> 00:03:50.760
These days, however, the circus no longer
employs a Child-Breaker.

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:56.400
Instead, the creation of new Clowns is the
responsibility of resident Clown Breeder,

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:57.870
Richard C. Normous.

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:02.470
And before you say anything, don't laugh,
that is his real name.

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:07.239
Some of the most famous Clowns in the troupe
are Eugene and Pius both of which are original

00:04:07.239 --> 00:04:13.270
Clowns, Mr. Noodles who is a bred Clown, and
Icky the troupe leader who was once a human

00:04:13.270 --> 00:04:17.019
with magical abilities known as Veronica Mason.

00:04:17.019 --> 00:04:21.759
She still possesses her anomalous powers as
Icky, and her magic act is one of the most

00:04:21.759 --> 00:04:24.599
beloved parts of our show.

00:04:24.599 --> 00:04:29.990
After the sudden disappearance of Herman Fuller,
Icky inherited his position as ringmaster,

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:33.789
and has been doing a spectacular job ever
since.

00:04:33.789 --> 00:04:37.770
Not every attempt to create new Clowns has
been as successful as Icky and Mr. Noodles

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:38.770
though.

00:04:38.770 --> 00:04:42.379
Some of the earlier attempts were quite grotesque
to look at.

00:04:42.379 --> 00:04:49.099
Herman Fuller's troupe of Clowns are an enthusiastic,
happy-go-lucky, but occasionally violent bunch,

00:04:49.099 --> 00:04:54.849
capable of minor feats of reality-bending
that allow them to perform all manner of tricks.

00:04:54.849 --> 00:04:59.800
They live on a diet of mostly sugar, and need
to be milked regularly.

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:04.050
Clown Milk is an invaluable substance here
at the circus, as it's the secret ingredient

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:09.009
of the famous black cotton candy - which,
by the way, is free with admission.

00:05:09.009 --> 00:05:14.009
It causes the brain to produce high levels
of serotonin, meaning that when you eat it,

00:05:14.009 --> 00:05:16.499
you're primed to have a great time.

00:05:16.499 --> 00:05:21.930
Be careful, though - raw, concentrated Clown
Milk is not for human consumption.

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:26.550
Though the Clowns love to drink it, even a
small amount can cause a human to go into

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:30.539
cardiac arrest due to an overload of happiness.

00:05:30.539 --> 00:05:35.529
The sound of calliope music also goes a long
way to helping people truly get the most out

00:05:35.529 --> 00:05:39.020
of their visit to Herman Fuller's Circus of
the Disquieting.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:43.689
The calliope is self-playing, and requires
rolls of perforated paper to be loaded into

00:05:43.689 --> 00:05:47.719
it so that it can play a variety of pre-programmed
pieces of music.

00:05:47.719 --> 00:05:51.870
Each piece produces a different psychological
effect on visitors who have consumed their

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:52.870
cotton candy.

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:57.270
“The Skater's Waltz” will make them accept
whatever they see at the circus, no matter

00:05:57.270 --> 00:06:00.679
how weird, as nothing out of the ordinary.

00:06:00.679 --> 00:06:06.270
Wonderful for making sure nobody blabs about
their experience to a certain pesky Foundation...

00:06:06.270 --> 00:06:11.669
”Officer of the Year” makes them less
likely to perceive an event as unlawful- we

00:06:11.669 --> 00:06:14.349
use that one when we suspect the cops are
closing in.

00:06:14.349 --> 00:06:15.349
“Hail!

00:06:15.349 --> 00:06:16.349
Hail!

00:06:16.349 --> 00:06:20.550
The Gang's All Here!” is used to get people
to congregate at the big top for showtime,

00:06:20.550 --> 00:06:24.860
and “American Patrol” causes those who
have eaten the cotton candy to seek out those

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:29.659
who haven't, in order to strongly encourage
them to have some.

00:06:29.659 --> 00:06:34.249
“What D'Ya Mean You Lost Your Dog?” is
one that gets played after hours, when it's

00:06:34.249 --> 00:06:36.819
time to get the clowns ready for milking.

00:06:36.819 --> 00:06:41.240
Now that you have an idea of the history and
how things work around the Circus, it’s

00:06:41.240 --> 00:06:43.039
time for the tour.

00:06:43.039 --> 00:06:48.110
The circus is made up of a series of tents
and trailers, as well as a midway with standard

00:06:48.110 --> 00:06:51.889
rides and games that you might find at any
circus.

00:06:51.889 --> 00:06:56.369
Outside of the Big Top, where shows are performed
once a day, there's also the Den of Freaks

00:06:56.369 --> 00:06:59.649
and the Hall of Humans Extraordinaire.

00:06:59.649 --> 00:07:05.750
The Den of Freaks is home to fantastic acts
like Sluggo, and Elisa the Living Head.

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:10.729
Sluggo is a man whose eyes are on stalks,
like those of a slug, and he can bend those

00:07:10.729 --> 00:07:13.330
stalks into any shape he wishes.

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:17.379
He can even use them to create the shapes
of human faces!

00:07:17.379 --> 00:07:22.080
Elisa the Living Head is a woman whose head
lives independently of her body, which is

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:24.309
safely kept in storage.

00:07:24.309 --> 00:07:29.589
Even without her body, she can speak and sing
and often answers questions from the audience.

00:07:29.589 --> 00:07:34.169
The Hall of Humans Extraordinaire is home
to performers who lack physical anomalies

00:07:34.169 --> 00:07:39.379
but otherwise display otherworldly talents
like The Amazing Zoltan, a fortune-teller

00:07:39.379 --> 00:07:43.990
and alchemist who Fuller picked up at a place
called the Utterly Bazaar.

00:07:43.990 --> 00:07:49.229
The Hall of Humans Extraordinaire also used
to be home to Icky the Clown, back when she

00:07:49.229 --> 00:07:51.929
was still Veronica the magician.

00:07:51.929 --> 00:07:56.999
The recent lineup has changed quite a bit,
thanks mainly to the activities of the Circus’s

00:07:56.999 --> 00:08:01.590
constant enemy - you guessed it, The SCP Foundation.

00:08:01.590 --> 00:08:06.319
Or as they are better known to the stable
of inter-dimensional clowns as the “Miss

00:08:06.319 --> 00:08:08.310
Essie P. Foundation”.

00:08:08.310 --> 00:08:12.709
The Foundation does not appear to be a fan
of circus folk, and many of the former acts

00:08:12.709 --> 00:08:14.800
are now in their containment.

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:24.649
For example, Madame Rezarta and her Amazing
Palm Reader, also known as SCP-1884-A and

00:08:24.649 --> 00:08:30.809
SCP-1884-B. Madame Rezarta was a blind Albanian
woman in her 60's who was born without hands.

00:08:30.809 --> 00:08:35.979
She shared a psychic link with a creature
named Luana, who was a large, shapeless entity

00:08:35.979 --> 00:08:38.690
made up of 932 hands.

00:08:38.690 --> 00:08:44.920
929 of these hands appear to be those of an
old woman, and share Madame Rezarta's DNA,

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:50.990
but the remaining 3 hands seem to be from
a male Caucasian adolescent, an adult Hispanic

00:08:50.990 --> 00:08:53.370
female, and a Bengal tiger.

00:08:53.370 --> 00:08:59.100
Through their psychic link, Luana acted as
Madame Rezarta's eyes, feeling its surroundings

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:01.870
to provide her with a mental map.

00:09:01.870 --> 00:09:06.209
Fuller attempted to buy the two of them when
they were 8 years old, but when their parents

00:09:06.209 --> 00:09:10.480
refused, he sent Manny to whisk them away
under the cover of darkness.

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:15.529
Madame Rezarta's act involved sending Luana
to feel the faces of audience members and

00:09:15.529 --> 00:09:19.990
then trying to describe their appearance based
on what Luana felt.

00:09:19.990 --> 00:09:25.259
The act was a hit, but Madame Rezarta claimed
to have been horribly abused during her time

00:09:25.259 --> 00:09:27.149
with Herman Fuller.

00:09:27.149 --> 00:09:31.980
The two of them escaped while on tour, and
were picked up by old’ Essie P. while trying

00:09:31.980 --> 00:09:34.480
to rent a hotel room in the UAE.

00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:39.399
Then, there's Virtuoso, also known as SCP-1860.

00:09:39.399 --> 00:09:44.130
Virtuoso was once a book of sheet music that
was transfigured by Herman Fuller into one

00:09:44.130 --> 00:09:46.250
of the circus' original acts.

00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:51.980
It's a tall, thin, humanoid being encased
in a densely woven paper-based material that

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:54.790
stretches like nylon or spandex.

00:09:54.790 --> 00:10:00.130
It constantly drips black ink… ink which
it has a telekinetic control over.

00:10:00.130 --> 00:10:06.019
It uses the ink to create the shapes of musical
notes, which float around it while it sings.

00:10:06.019 --> 00:10:11.709
Virtuoso can sing in multiple voices at once
across different vocal ranges, and constantly

00:10:11.709 --> 00:10:16.069
performs arias and showtunes for whoever is
listening.

00:10:16.069 --> 00:10:20.450
It was recovered from underneath a burnt-down
shack at a fairground where the circus had

00:10:20.450 --> 00:10:21.639
been set up earlier.

00:10:21.639 --> 00:10:27.069
In containment, Virtuoso still sings, but
translations from Italian reveal that the

00:10:27.069 --> 00:10:32.579
lyrics of the arias it's singing have been
changed to reflect its own situation.

00:10:32.579 --> 00:10:38.370
Some of these translated lyrics include- “One
day I'll tell you of my creation, and life

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:43.829
with the circus, born from the ringmaster,
his breed”

00:10:43.829 --> 00:10:49.800
Another act the circus dearly misses is Motormouth,
also known as SCP-2094.

00:10:49.800 --> 00:10:54.509
He was one of the rare human clowns, born
in New York City in the late 70's.

00:10:54.509 --> 00:10:59.899
From birth, he displayed a supernatural level
of flexibility in his lower jaw, and as he

00:10:59.899 --> 00:11:04.699
grew older he discovered that he could swallow
large objects and store them in a kind of

00:11:04.699 --> 00:11:08.860
pocket dimension until he needed them again.

00:11:08.860 --> 00:11:14.029
Unlike Madame Rezarta, he went with Manny
willingly, as even at 8 years old he knew

00:11:14.029 --> 00:11:18.329
his alcoholic mother didn't care if he lived
or died.

00:11:18.329 --> 00:11:22.899
Motormouth took to the circus like a fish
to water, and grew from a shy child into a

00:11:22.899 --> 00:11:27.089
very talented, talkative, and highly charismatic
adult.

00:11:27.089 --> 00:11:31.160
He was a juggler, first and foremost, who
would catch pins, balls and knives in his

00:11:31.160 --> 00:11:35.899
mouth as part of his routine, but the name
“Motormouth” came later in his career

00:11:35.899 --> 00:11:40.839
when he let a stunt driver drive a car off
a ramp and down his throat.

00:11:40.839 --> 00:11:48.209
However, as great an act as he was, a conflict
arose between him and Manny over Manny's questionable

00:11:48.209 --> 00:11:51.250
methods of sourcing new acts.

00:11:51.250 --> 00:11:55.399
Manny found out that Motormouth had been helping
some of the anomalous kids that Manny brought

00:11:55.399 --> 00:12:00.680
in get back to their families, and as punishment
for his insubordination, he was locked in

00:12:00.680 --> 00:12:05.370
a box and left behind at the end of a Japanese
tour.

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:10.329
The box was marked 'For Essie', because Manny
thought being put in containment was the best

00:12:10.329 --> 00:12:12.480
punishment he could think of.

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:17.720
With how strange and unusual its acts are,
and how it always seems to pop in and out

00:12:17.720 --> 00:12:23.990
of new locations at strange, unpredictable
times, you might wonder if the Circus has

00:12:23.990 --> 00:12:25.819
any sinister motives.

00:12:25.819 --> 00:12:31.230
Well, the truth is, though sometimes the acts
can be a little gruesome, their methods of

00:12:31.230 --> 00:12:38.060
acquiring new talent a little unorthodox,
and the clowns a little out of control, their

00:12:38.060 --> 00:12:40.990
only goal… is to entertain.

00:12:40.990 --> 00:12:45.339
In that respect, they’re no better or worse
than any other circus.

00:12:45.339 --> 00:12:47.579
So, we hope you've enjoyed your visit.

00:12:47.579 --> 00:12:51.850
Make sure to stick around for the show, and
don't forget to take your complimentary serving

00:12:51.850 --> 00:12:53.760
of cotton candy.

00:12:53.760 --> 00:13:00.240
Because there's nothing quite like a day at
the circus, especially one like Herman Fuller's.

00:13:00.240 --> 00:13:06.660
Now check out “SCP Chaos Insurgency Explained”
and “Secret Group That Runs The World - SCP

00:13:06.660 --> 00:13:14.389
O5 Council Explained” for more mysterious
groups from the world of the SCP Foundation!

